WEBVTT


00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.646
You're going to be on live. Okay.


00:00:12.603 --> 00:00:17.745
Ready in three, two, one...


00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:21.756
This is Sharon Solomon with a Channel 6
News exclusive story.


00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:24.348
One that some might say
is out of this world.


00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:28.384
I am here live at the perimeter of
the Air Force Flight Test Center.


00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:31.795
And if that sounds unfamiliar to you,
then perhaps you know this base


00:00:31.853 --> 00:00:34.458
by its more popular name, Area 51.


00:00:35.055 --> 00:00:39.003
Rumored to be a classified holding area
for alien life forms,


00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:42.699
Area 51 is widely known as the most
secretive place on Earth,


00:00:43.096 --> 00:00:47.738
but we at Channel' 6 have just f earned
today that the government has given in


00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.710
to public and political pressure


00:00:49.768 --> 00:00:53.511
and is allowing visitors to Area 51
for the first time ever.


00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:56.645
This is Sharon Solomon, reporting live.
Now back to you.


00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:39.118
I want this to go quickly and cleanly.


00:01:39.678 --> 00:01:41.351
Two hours, tops.


00:01:41.981 --> 00:01:43.460
I will take them around Level 1,


00:01:43.515 --> 00:01:46.360
but Level 2 is more important
to our tour here.


00:01:46.685 --> 00:01:50.655
Our guests must feel they saw something
that no one has ever seen before.


00:01:51.089 --> 00:01:53.729
If they go back and report
that there is no access,


00:01:54.058 --> 00:01:59.904
no transparency at Area 51,
my superiors will make my life hell.


00:01:59.962 --> 00:02:04.069
Which means I will have no choice
but to make all of your lives hell


00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.510
so I'll have company.


00:02:06.502 --> 00:02:07.605
Understand?


00:02:09.639 --> 00:02:11.208
All right.


00:02:20.448 --> 00:02:24.328
You all know this man.
For 20 years, World Report Nightly.


00:02:24.618 --> 00:02:27.291
"I'm Sam Whitaker and that is the news."


00:02:30.656 --> 00:02:32.227
That is correct.


00:02:34.893 --> 00:02:37.032
But he's not the one
we're concerned with here.


00:02:40.365 --> 00:02:46.837
Claire Fallen. Author, creator
and sole contributor to The Fact Zone,


00:02:48.072 --> 00:02:50.813
the world's most popular news blog.


00:02:54.376 --> 00:02:57.653
Fallen was added to the tour, last minute,
over my objections.


00:02:59.615 --> 00:03:02.356
Remember, shoot everything.


00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:03.795
Always do.


00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:09.426
Boys in Washington hope her street cred
will help dispel these stories


00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.732
of us hiding extraterrestrials here.


00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.669
I caught your appearance
on Talk Back last week.


00:03:14.895 --> 00:03:17.534
Cool. Did you learn anything?


00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:22.703
Both reporters will be bringing along
an assistant to document the tour.


00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:31.815
Here on a skeleton crew shift,
our guests may take a look around


00:03:31.876 --> 00:03:33.982
and think they can get away with something


00:03:34.045 --> 00:03:36.820
simply because no one
seems to be watching.


00:03:37.915 --> 00:03:40.554
That's why I want you all
to be extra vigilant.


00:03:41.986 --> 00:03:46.934
If any of these four guests
get anywhere near the lower levels,


00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:52.495
you are authorized to shoot them first
and make up the reasons why later.


00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.536
You know the drill. Make me proud.


00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.575
- Dismissed.
- Yes, sir.


00:04:38.768 --> 00:04:41.941
Wow. I can't believe
that Claire Fallon's here.


00:04:42.737 --> 00:04:45.082
You think the Chief will let me
get my picture taken with her?


00:04:45.141 --> 00:04:47.177
Yeah, because the Chief loves it
when people leave their posts


00:04:47.242 --> 00:04:48.516
to go hit on reporters.


00:04:51.379 --> 00:04:55.087
Welcome to Area 51.
I am Colonel Ronald Martin.


00:04:55.149 --> 00:04:57.890
I will be your tour guide today.


00:04:57.951 --> 00:04:59.727
I want to thank you all for coming.


00:04:59.787 --> 00:05:01.356
I assure you that my superiors


00:05:01.421 --> 00:05:06.336
wish for today's event
to represent a new sense of honesty


00:05:06.392 --> 00:05:10.032
and transparency
between the government and the public.


00:05:12.264 --> 00:05:14.107
Isn’t she the one that...


00:05:14.166 --> 00:05:15.702
Yeah.


00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:20.010
Now, our base here
is a six-by-10-mile installation


00:05:20.071 --> 00:05:25.315
with a rich history of military progress
in the areas of aviation and weaponry,


00:05:26.109 --> 00:05:31.081
backed by a strong sense of tradition,
honor, and pride.


00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.051
I got a question.


00:05:36.117 --> 00:05:38.621
We've been posted at this nest
for over a year...


00:05:40.288 --> 00:05:41.767
That's not a question.


00:05:41.823 --> 00:05:45.270
Well, the question is what's the point?


00:05:50.097 --> 00:05:52.832
Shoes, are you an enlisted man
in the United States Air Force?


00:05:52.833 --> 00:05:55.278
- Yeah.
- Do you follow those orders?


00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:57.280
- Yeah.
- That's the point.


00:05:57.603 --> 00:06:01.881
But since all of you
are only interested in one thing,


00:06:02.041 --> 00:06:07.991
we will forgo a proper tour of the base
and focus on what you came here for.


00:06:10.781 --> 00:06:12.385
Hangar 18.


00:06:15.518 --> 00:06:17.226
Follow me, please.


00:06:20.023 --> 00:06:21.832
I'd still like to meet her, though.


00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:31.934
- Lieutenant Walters?
- Yes, sir.


00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:35.305
I heard they were transferring you over
from the Malaka Pod pens.


00:06:35.403 --> 00:06:38.349
This tour's got everyone moving around.


00:06:38.405 --> 00:06:41.909
Boy, if those guests could only see
what's really down here.


00:06:42.542 --> 00:06:43.577
Yes, sir.


00:06:44.511 --> 00:06:47.219
I'm a civilian, Walters.
You don't have to call me sir.


00:06:47.347 --> 00:06:50.327
- Understand?
- Yes, civilian.


00:06:51.283 --> 00:06:52.887
Doc will be just fine.


00:06:53.017 --> 00:06:54.155
Ground rules.


00:06:54.218 --> 00:06:59.224
What you see here is proprietary technology
decommissioned specifically for this tour.


00:06:59.657 --> 00:07:02.160
You may report on what I show you,


00:07:02.226 --> 00:07:05.365
but if I ask you not to shoot
something or to write about it,


00:07:05.429 --> 00:07:07.466
you will oblige. Are we clear?


00:07:08.431 --> 00:07:11.606
Look but don't touch,
always stay with the group,


00:07:12.301 --> 00:07:14.713
and if you should stray from the tour,


00:07:16.171 --> 00:07:20.085
Lieutenant Kamecki, here,
will help you find your way back.


00:07:27.515 --> 00:07:31.326
The subject you're about to encounter
crash-landed 25 years ago.


00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.120
He's not like the others you've seen.


00:07:33.954 --> 00:07:37.059
He's a morpher. You know what that means?


00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:40.126
He changes shapes.
Anyone he touches, he can imitate.


00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:43.571
Sorry, you wanted him to answer.


00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:51.803
His DNA has a replicating element.
it simulates skin, clothes, hair.


00:07:52.803 --> 00:07:55.146
If he touches you, he can look like you.


00:07:56.173 --> 00:07:59.676
He can speak like you, too,
but only things he's heard you say.


00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:05.623
In fact, at anytime he can look or sound
like anyone he's ever imitated.


00:08:06.849 --> 00:08:08.624
Are you ready to meet Patient Zero?


00:08:30.536 --> 00:08:33.516
Right. I got it. Mindy, and here.
Mindy? Here.


00:08:33.772 --> 00:08:36.720
So, Colonel, tell us
why is this called Area 51?


00:08:38.643 --> 00:08:42.180
Old land survey maps were broken down
into geo-grids.


00:08:42.246 --> 00:08:46.353
So where we are now is situated
on a square numbered 51.


00:08:46.784 --> 00:08:49.855
- In fact...
- Colonel, if I may,


00:08:49.919 --> 00:08:52.560
is it really just you and this kid
taking us on this tour?


00:08:52.623 --> 00:08:53.726
I mean, no offense, sir.


00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.963
It's just I would have thought
that for such a landmark event...


00:08:56.025 --> 00:08:57.526
Miss Fallen,


00:08:59.061 --> 00:09:02.234
you'll understand the U.S. Military
has important jobs to do.


00:09:02.297 --> 00:09:05.277
Now, if we were really keeping
extraterrestrials here,


00:09:05.332 --> 00:09:09.974
it might qualify as an important job.
But we're not, so it doesn't.


00:09:10.437 --> 00:09:12.041
Now, don't get me wrong,


00:09:12.106 --> 00:09:15.417
you'll see very many impressive things
on this tour,


00:09:15.476 --> 00:09:19.013
but there are no aliens
to be found in Area 51.


00:09:34.258 --> 00:09:36.203
What do we do if he tries something?


00:09:36.727 --> 00:09:38.468
25 years, a model patient.


00:09:39.462 --> 00:09:42.068
But if he does try something, shoot him.


00:09:44.501 --> 00:09:46.538
Why isn't he in restraints?


00:09:47.436 --> 00:09:50.246
The restraints make him depressed
and uncooperative.


00:09:50.306 --> 00:09:54.845
We figured out away to keep his mood up
with a regimen of gaseous drugs


00:09:54.909 --> 00:09:57.116
absorbed through his skin.


00:09:58.846 --> 00:10:03.386
We synthesize the sedative using
his own blood mixed with human blood.


00:10:03.617 --> 00:10:07.029
His is blue.
That's why the gas comes out purple.


00:10:08.355 --> 00:10:10.062
We try to keep him happy.


00:10:11.424 --> 00:10:15.338
Two meals a day and his favorite band
on a loop.


00:10:16.229 --> 00:10:18.469
What is it? Some kind of alien music?


00:10:19.331 --> 00:10:22.675
Actually, the band is called Ice Spiders.


00:10:22.733 --> 00:10:25.271
They're from Earth.
Well, as far as we know.


00:10:25.337 --> 00:10:28.078
Patient Zero spends most of his time here


00:10:28.138 --> 00:10:31.415
and sometimes we do use him
on special jobs.


00:10:31.508 --> 00:10:34.351
My dad has that same picture of Reagan.


00:10:34.677 --> 00:10:36.486
It's not Reagan.


00:10:42.184 --> 00:10:46.724
Lunch time.
And how is my favorite patient today?


00:10:50.658 --> 00:10:52.194
Sorry about this.


00:11:13.945 --> 00:11:15.151
It’s okay.


00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:22.089
There you go. it's good, isn't it?


00:12:01.253 --> 00:12:02.356
J Rod, are you there?


00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:08.136
J Rod, I'm detecting some unusual behavior
in Little Devil's pen.


00:12:08.492 --> 00:12:12.030
It's probably nothing, but if you get
a second can you check his vitals?


00:12:12.697 --> 00:12:15.870
All right. it's probably nothing,
but I will check.


00:12:16.132 --> 00:12:17.543
Thanks, good buddy.


00:12:42.823 --> 00:12:44.632
Welcome to the Warehouse.


00:12:53.965 --> 00:12:57.606
This is the POW.


00:12:58.703 --> 00:13:01.842
- The POW?
- Pulse Operated Weapon.


00:13:02.606 --> 00:13:05.678
Creates an aimed impacted
equivalent to 10 grenades.


00:13:05.976 --> 00:13:08.615
Has it been...
Has it been used yet in combat?


00:13:10.646 --> 00:13:13.252
The first set doesn't come off-line
until next year.


00:13:13.316 --> 00:13:14.920
We hope it won't have to be.


00:13:16.018 --> 00:13:20.193
This weapon is so accurate.
It has a three-mile range.


00:13:27.361 --> 00:13:30.433
We've got 3,000 of these things
ready for service.


00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:37.707
Whoa! How are you doing, buddy?


00:13:40.039 --> 00:13:41.450
Nice place.


00:13:44.276 --> 00:13:45.755
Do you ever talk?


00:13:46.978 --> 00:13:52.155
I know 62 ways to kill a man,
and you're barely a man.


00:13:55.252 --> 00:13:57.095
If my men don't die, I'm a happy man.


00:14:03.592 --> 00:14:05.299
I don't think he likes me.


00:14:19.606 --> 00:14:21.483
What the hell is going on down there?


00:14:43.627 --> 00:14:44.832
Oh, no.


00:14:51.167 --> 00:14:52.770
No! No! No!


00:14:52.835 --> 00:14:55.282
Doc! Hang on. It could be a trap.


00:14:55.338 --> 00:14:58.147
That's why you're here. Let's go.


00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:06.219
It’s okay. it's okay.
it's okay. Stay with me.


00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.122
I've got you.


00:15:15.988 --> 00:15:17.297
It’s okay.


00:15:20.159 --> 00:15:22.935
Shoot him! Shoot him!


00:15:22.995 --> 00:15:24.702
Wait! Wait!


00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.046
Wait! Wait!


00:15:41.411 --> 00:15:42.446
Oh, no.


00:16:01.295 --> 00:16:03.275
Hey, Gomez. I think we're okay down here.


00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:05.173
Yeah. It looks like they've settled down.


00:16:05.232 --> 00:16:07.142
I'm going to send down J Rod
for a check-up.


00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.779
Well, all right.


00:16:11.437 --> 00:16:15.384
Dr. Keane, it's Gomez.
Did you take care of Patient Zero?


00:16:16.074 --> 00:16:19.351
Dr. Keane? Dr. Keane, are you reading me?


00:16:22.079 --> 00:16:24.992
- J Rod, are you there?
- Yes, I am here.


00:16:25.582 --> 00:16:28.291
- Can I get a read...
- it's okay. it's okay.


00:16:28.352 --> 00:16:30.797
I was just... Where have you been?
I've been looking...


00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.738
it's good, isn't it?


00:16:45.033 --> 00:16:49.243
Apologies, Lieutenant Gomez.
I did not hear the end of your question.


00:16:51.573 --> 00:16:54.451
Sorry. it's good. it's okay.


00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.646
Very well.


00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.057
So here's my theory.


00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.532
I think everything we do here
is just window dressing.


00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.092
Stop thinking. You're bad at it.


00:17:13.158 --> 00:17:15.069
Well, if everything on display here
was state of the art,


00:17:15.126 --> 00:17:16.627
it would be obvious
we're hiding something important.


00:17:17.027 --> 00:17:18.529
It’s a classic poker move.


00:17:20.998 --> 00:17:22.944
If you're holding something strong,
you represent weakness.


00:17:23.067 --> 00:17:24.477
We're assigned to an ancient weapon


00:17:24.534 --> 00:17:26.377
'cause there's actually nothing here
worth defending.


00:17:26.803 --> 00:17:29.113
We should be grateful,
'cause this provides us with a guarantee


00:17:29.172 --> 00:17:31.481
that nobody will ever shoot at us.


00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.486
And who are you
to talk about poker strategy


00:17:33.542 --> 00:17:35.145
after I took 50 bucks off you last weekend?


00:17:35.209 --> 00:17:36.689
Hey! You got lucky.


00:17:37.379 --> 00:17:38.914
You cried like a baby.


00:17:39.313 --> 00:17:40.849
Airmen don't cry.


00:17:40.915 --> 00:17:42.894
- They bleed tears.
- They bleed tears. Yeah.


00:17:44.752 --> 00:17:46.595
Thank God. Let's go grab some grub.


00:18:06.638 --> 00:18:09.846
Hey, Gomez?
I Ain’t got a degree in aliens or nothing,


00:18:09.906 --> 00:18:12.216
but I think there's something wrong
with one of these guys.


00:18:12.976 --> 00:18:16.685
Are you gonna send J Rod
down here or what?


00:18:17.247 --> 00:18:20.591
Lady Death hit her gate pretty hard.
We better make sure she...


00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:23.062
Gomez, what the hell?
Did you open up Little Devil's gate?


00:19:09.426 --> 00:19:10.905
That's amazing.


00:19:11.227 --> 00:19:13.968
I mean, I can count the leaves
in my swimming pool.


00:19:15.564 --> 00:19:19.068
What about you, Claire?
Want to see your backyard from space?


00:19:19.134 --> 00:19:20.976
You can see my house on Google Earth.


00:19:21.169 --> 00:19:25.948
Not with this clarity.
You really need to trim these hedges.


00:19:28.608 --> 00:19:30.178
Detecting a life form.


00:19:31.511 --> 00:19:33.081
My friend Astrid is cat sitting.


00:19:33.447 --> 00:19:35.687
She's talking on the phone.
You want to hear what she's saying?


00:19:37.583 --> 00:19:41.156
Two best sellers
and a big advance on the next one.


00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.165
Trust me, her place is gorgeous.


00:19:43.221 --> 00:19:48.193
It's just sad that she has no one to share
it with except for all these cats.


00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:53.139
Colonel, forgive me, but you have
to assure me that the U.S. government


00:19:53.197 --> 00:19:55.609
is not using this technology
to spy on U.S. citizens.


00:19:55.666 --> 00:20:00.205
The government is not using this
technology to spy on our citizens yet.


00:20:02.605 --> 00:20:03.709
Claire?


00:20:07.576 --> 00:20:10.420
Well, Claire, you have no pending
arrest warrants


00:20:10.712 --> 00:20:13.318
and your facial structure
indicates only a two percent chance


00:20:13.714 --> 00:20:16.388
of you ever carrying out
a terrorist attack.


00:20:20.187 --> 00:20:23.190
And you were in Afghanistan
sometime in the last month?


00:20:23.456 --> 00:20:24.901
How the hell would it know that?


00:20:26.559 --> 00:20:29.835
The software provides
"skin texturing analysis,


00:20:29.895 --> 00:20:31.670
"reveals recent weathering


00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.609
"due to environmental elements
unique to Kabul."


00:20:35.701 --> 00:20:37.839
The bigger question is
why didn't I know about it?


00:20:37.902 --> 00:20:40.473
That should have come out
when we vetted you.


00:20:40.538 --> 00:20:42.984
Well, it was a secret trip.


00:20:45.675 --> 00:20:47.712
Well, cherish your secrets, Claire.


00:20:47.778 --> 00:20:50.190
The future brings us
fewer and fewer of them.


00:20:50.714 --> 00:20:52.750
What about your secrets, Colonel?


00:20:57.353 --> 00:20:59.526
I know you're not telling us everything.


00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.799
Is that what you want?


00:21:04.058 --> 00:21:07.733
You truly believe that civilians
need a window on the military?


00:21:07.795 --> 00:21:09.365
Has it ever occurred to you


00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:12.274
that if the American public knew
what we were up to, so would our enemies?


00:21:12.332 --> 00:21:15.972
Actually, sir,
that's exactly what's occurred to me.


00:21:17.036 --> 00:21:20.916
I don't think that you've let us in
because you caved to public pressure.


00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:26.953
I think all this is your way of exploiting
journalists as de facto Psy-Ops agents.


00:21:27.446 --> 00:21:29.517
You plant the stories you want us to write,


00:21:29.581 --> 00:21:32.220
we distribute your propaganda
free of charge,


00:21:32.283 --> 00:21:37.631
and hostile foreign governments quietly
take note of the U.S. military's might.


00:21:39.055 --> 00:21:42.093
I mean, maybe Libya and Syria will think
twice about how they deal with us


00:21:42.158 --> 00:21:44.968
if their leaders believe that
we have a high-yield chemical laser


00:21:45.028 --> 00:21:48.236
that can vaporize a human target
from space.


00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:55.506
I don't know if you have aliens here, sir,
but I do know you have secrets.


00:21:55.703 --> 00:22:00.777
And it's time the public knew the truth.
All due respect.


00:22:03.443 --> 00:22:06.788
Well said. But you've got one thing wrong.


00:22:06.847 --> 00:22:11.818
It’s not about what I want.
I answer to superiors. I follow orders.


00:22:11.984 --> 00:22:15.727
You, you write about whatever
you wanton your blog.


00:22:15.788 --> 00:22:16.926
You answer to no one.


00:22:17.356 --> 00:22:20.427
You bear the full responsibility
of everything you do that is right,


00:22:20.492 --> 00:22:23.405
and everything you do that is wrong.


00:22:23.461 --> 00:22:25.963
We all do, Colonel. Every last one of us.


00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:31.640
Excuse me.


00:22:32.969 --> 00:22:34.277
This is Colonel Martin.


00:22:34.871 --> 00:22:36.407
Yes, I did.


00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:39.849
No. Of course not. I...


00:22:40.543 --> 00:22:43.250
What? No, I didn't agree to...


00:22:52.920 --> 00:22:54.331
Yes, sir, understood.


00:22:59.392 --> 00:23:01.394
How many levels are there?


00:23:02.028 --> 00:23:03.132
Two.


00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:07.536
Somebody is watching us, aren't they?


00:23:18.943 --> 00:23:20.478
You're not coming with us?


00:23:20.544 --> 00:23:21.818
I've been ordered not to.


00:23:21.945 --> 00:23:23.549
Who the hell was on that call?


00:23:31.387 --> 00:23:33.526
I think they bought it.


00:23:47.868 --> 00:23:49.347
I'm telling you, they're here.


00:23:49.436 --> 00:23:52.780
And not just on this Earth.
They're right here on this base.


00:23:52.905 --> 00:23:55.181
Here he goes again with
his little green men.


00:23:55.274 --> 00:23:57.481
Gray. Well, at least the ones
at Roswell were.


00:23:57.577 --> 00:23:58.953
And Rendlesham.


00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:01.685
Not really sure about the ones
at Kecksburg, though, but I do suspect.


00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:04.788
Dude, you read too many comic books.


00:24:04.849 --> 00:24:07.351
Yeah? Well, you ever learn to read,
I'll share them with you.


00:24:07.418 --> 00:24:10.695
Cork it, boys. You know how the chief
feels about wild speculation.


00:24:11.722 --> 00:24:13.258
He's against it.


00:24:14.190 --> 00:24:18.002
Well, I can tell you this much,
if the aliens ever do come to get us,


00:24:18.127 --> 00:24:20.505
I ain't trusting you to
fight them off for us.


00:24:24.166 --> 00:24:26.373
What's that supposed to mean?


00:24:26.835 --> 00:24:27.870
That's enough, Travis.


00:24:28.337 --> 00:24:31.283
Well, I'm just saying when it's go time,
you shoot the enemy.


00:24:31.339 --> 00:24:33.046
Not your own damn foot.


00:24:35.376 --> 00:24:37.013
You want to go? You want to go with me?


00:24:37.944 --> 00:24:39.389
I don't hit cowards.


00:24:41.615 --> 00:24:43.788
- I said that's enough.
- He started it.


00:24:44.450 --> 00:24:46.487
You're looking at a higher rank, Airman.


00:24:46.785 --> 00:24:48.787
You don't shut up,
you're going to have to deal with me.


00:24:50.856 --> 00:24:53.096
I don't hit fake heroes, either.


00:24:53.858 --> 00:24:55.736
Hey! Hey! Don't...


00:24:55.794 --> 00:24:56.828
Attention!


00:25:04.067 --> 00:25:05.239
You got something we need
to talk about, Travis?


00:25:05.302 --> 00:25:06.303
Negative, Chief.


00:25:10.573 --> 00:25:12.246
- What about you, Schumacher?
- Yeah. He's...


00:25:13.776 --> 00:25:14.914
Negative, Chief.


00:25:18.914 --> 00:25:22.019
You're a leader. Try and act like it.


00:25:22.651 --> 00:25:24.254
Yes, Chief.


00:25:29.323 --> 00:25:30.926
At ease, Airmen.


00:26:21.435 --> 00:26:24.314
You think we shouldn't have let
them go down there unescorted?


00:26:24.371 --> 00:26:26.145
Sir, what I think doesn't matter, sir.


00:26:26.205 --> 00:26:29.277
No, no. Speak freely, Kamecki.


00:26:30.976 --> 00:26:33.046
I don't think they should be here at all.


00:26:33.111 --> 00:26:35.819
I don't want them
within 100 miles of this base.


00:26:36.248 --> 00:26:38.227
Public poking they noses into our business!


00:26:38.283 --> 00:26:39.785
- They should be thanking God that we...
- Stop.


00:26:39.851 --> 00:26:42.694
Stop speaking freely, Kamecki.


00:26:52.929 --> 00:26:54.067
Yeah, Dr. Haven?


00:26:54.764 --> 00:26:56.037
I need you in the lab right now.


00:26:56.131 --> 00:26:57.906
Yes, sir. Right away.


00:26:58.100 --> 00:27:00.239
Bring along the Angel Eyes
camera system with you


00:27:00.302 --> 00:27:01.372
and pretend you're working on it.


00:27:01.870 --> 00:27:03.940
Make like it's a big secret.


00:27:04.572 --> 00:27:06.017
Yes, sir.


00:27:07.409 --> 00:27:08.910
Wear a white lab coat.


00:27:09.110 --> 00:27:10.646
It completes the image.


00:27:10.945 --> 00:27:14.050
Yes, of course, sir. I'm already on it.


00:27:17.083 --> 00:27:19.358
Dr. Keane. I was just heading...


00:28:07.126 --> 00:28:11.973
Hi. Hi. We weren't really
prepared for this,


00:28:12.031 --> 00:28:15.170
but Colonel Martin
mentioned something that...


00:28:16.034 --> 00:28:18.571
Wow. You're Sam Whitaker.


00:28:18.670 --> 00:28:20.377
Yeah. it's nice to meet you
and don't mind us.


00:28:20.438 --> 00:28:21.711
We're just here to observe.


00:28:22.239 --> 00:28:24.150
Okay. Great. Sure.


00:28:25.843 --> 00:28:32.055
Just give me a moment and
I'll show you something really cool.


00:28:36.652 --> 00:28:38.188
You buying this?


00:28:38.253 --> 00:28:40.324
No. Just browsing.


00:28:53.633 --> 00:28:54.805
Looking for the shot?


00:28:56.603 --> 00:28:58.139
What shot?


00:28:58.471 --> 00:29:00.916
The shot. The one that everyone will see.


00:29:01.607 --> 00:29:03.712
The raising of the flag at Iwo Jima?


00:29:03.909 --> 00:29:07.446
The naked Vietnamese napalm girl?
See, that's the shot that I want.


00:29:07.512 --> 00:29:10.926
The one that millions will see
long after I'm dead.


00:29:13.585 --> 00:29:15.120
That's not what I'm looking for.


00:29:18.423 --> 00:29:19.901
What are you looking for?


00:29:24.627 --> 00:29:28.370
When I was a little girl,
my brother woke me up one night


00:29:28.431 --> 00:29:31.570
and told me that aliens
were landing outside.


00:29:31.833 --> 00:29:37.545
And he rushed me out and showed me dozens
of bright streaks all across the sky.


00:29:37.606 --> 00:29:40.916
- He was just messing with you.
- Well, yeah. It was a meteor shower.


00:29:40.975 --> 00:29:43.785
But I don't know.
I still look up in the sky and I think,


00:29:45.212 --> 00:29:49.159
"We can't be alone. No, they're coming."


00:29:50.783 --> 00:29:52.387
If they haven't already.


00:29:53.720 --> 00:29:56.893
That's why I'm here. Why are you here?


00:29:58.957 --> 00:30:00.334
Looking for the shot.


00:30:04.128 --> 00:30:05.607
- You're all set with that?
- Yeah, ready.


00:30:05.663 --> 00:30:08.041
Shoot away. Fire at will.


00:30:10.700 --> 00:30:15.740
So, why did you go on national television
and call me a corporate puddle?


00:30:16.339 --> 00:30:20.116
I didn't. I called you a tabloid traitor.


00:30:21.343 --> 00:30:22.822
Well. That's much better.


00:30:24.779 --> 00:30:27.350
But you cannot raise standards
from the outside.


00:30:28.217 --> 00:30:32.721
I'm in it every day doing everything I can
to make a difference.


00:30:32.853 --> 00:30:36.630
You work for a network whose slogan
is "We go beyond the headlines."


00:30:37.224 --> 00:30:38.294
And?


00:30:38.458 --> 00:30:40.028
It’s your job to go beyond the headlines.


00:30:40.160 --> 00:30:43.140
It’s like Betty Crocker saying,
"We make food you can eat."


00:30:43.430 --> 00:30:46.706
You don't think that I fight with my bosses
every day so that I can report on stories


00:30:46.766 --> 00:30:47.836
that damn well matter?


00:30:48.033 --> 00:30:51.277
No. I just think
you're not fighting hard enough.


00:30:57.942 --> 00:31:02.584
Okay. So, you mind if I give you
a piece of advice?


00:31:03.180 --> 00:31:04.522
Please. I can't wait.


00:31:04.580 --> 00:31:07.288
- You keep challenging the Colonel.
- And?


00:31:07.417 --> 00:31:10.523
And you don't get the real story
by attacking your subject.


00:31:10.586 --> 00:31:14.466
You befriend him.
You make him feel comfortable.


00:31:14.724 --> 00:31:19.034
You earn his trust and then you coax
out of him what you really need.


00:31:28.568 --> 00:31:31.481
So why do you think
he let us loose down here?


00:31:31.538 --> 00:31:33.074
I think it's a chess game


00:31:33.139 --> 00:31:35.914
and I think the Colonel knew
that we were not playing his game,


00:31:35.975 --> 00:31:37.751
and so he made a move
that we didn't expect.


00:31:37.811 --> 00:31:42.121
He gave us something we wanted
in hopes to gain something even bigger.


00:31:46.851 --> 00:31:49.730
Haven should have been there by now.


00:31:50.120 --> 00:31:52.566
So either there's nothing down here
to discover,


00:31:52.622 --> 00:31:54.761
or he knows we won't discover it.


00:31:54.858 --> 00:31:58.327
Well, but maybe there's a third option.
Maybe there is something to discover.


00:31:59.295 --> 00:32:01.367
And the colonel wants us to discover it.


00:32:03.532 --> 00:32:07.001
So you mean he wants us to find something.
He just can't give it to us.


00:32:09.038 --> 00:32:10.641
I mean, yeah.


00:32:11.673 --> 00:32:12.708
Maybe.


00:32:15.009 --> 00:32:17.319
Okay. We're ready.


00:32:19.146 --> 00:32:21.955
Three, two, one...


00:32:22.849 --> 00:32:24.386
Yeah.


00:32:30.989 --> 00:32:33.595
I don't get it.


00:32:33.859 --> 00:32:35.065
Look closer.


00:32:42.466 --> 00:32:44.103
It’s an invisibility shield.


00:32:44.701 --> 00:32:48.114
It's wrapping light around my arm
so that you only perceive the light


00:32:48.171 --> 00:32:52.016
from behind the arm,
making it appear to disappear.


00:32:52.307 --> 00:32:55.811
Oh, my God!
I knew they'd have this technology,


00:32:55.878 --> 00:32:57.152
but I had no idea that it was...


00:32:57.212 --> 00:32:59.453
No, no, no, I had no...
I mean, this is much more advanced...


00:32:59.514 --> 00:33:00.822
But see, what the really neat thing is...


00:33:00.882 --> 00:33:03.761
All right. Listen up.
Everyone needs to evacuate the area


00:33:03.818 --> 00:33:06.025
- and return to ground level.
- Why? Colonel, what's going on?


00:33:06.087 --> 00:33:07.429
I'll explain later upstairs.


00:33:07.487 --> 00:33:09.831
- You turn that off. Now.
- Hang on. Why can't we...


00:33:09.890 --> 00:33:11.062
- Now listen, Miss Fallen...
- What?


00:33:11.124 --> 00:33:14.196
My priority is to get
my valued scientists to safety.


00:33:14.261 --> 00:33:16.763
Now, if you and the rest of the tour group
make it, that's fine with me.


00:33:16.829 --> 00:33:18.366
Let go of me.


00:33:58.365 --> 00:34:00.675
No! No! No!


00:34:16.582 --> 00:34:20.791
Everybody out! Go on. Go!
Get out of here! Go! Go!


00:34:42.537 --> 00:34:44.676
You still upset about what Travis said?


00:34:46.040 --> 00:34:49.782
What's there to be upset about?
He was right. I'm a fake hero.


00:34:51.778 --> 00:34:53.018
You know the story.


00:34:54.448 --> 00:34:55.983
Yeah.


00:34:57.683 --> 00:35:00.323
What you didn't read
was how they sold it to me.


00:35:00.386 --> 00:35:02.525
Drugged up,
lying in a hospital bed in Germany.


00:35:02.588 --> 00:35:06.092
Some military journalist hovering over me,
pitching me a story.


00:35:07.425 --> 00:35:09.564
"Female airman shot down in war zone.


00:35:10.028 --> 00:35:14.033
"Sole survivor empties her gun fighting off
enemy troops with a broken arm.


00:35:15.266 --> 00:35:18.509
"Escapes on foot.
Rescues wounded orphan on the way."


00:35:18.569 --> 00:35:19.672
Well, you did get shot down.


00:35:20.870 --> 00:35:24.943
And you are female.
At least they got that right.


00:35:28.644 --> 00:35:34.151
My shoulder was sprained.
I never broke my arm. I never fired my gun.


00:35:35.082 --> 00:35:37.723
I just ran, fast as I could.


00:35:39.587 --> 00:35:43.591
Kid was on the same chopper as me.
I was holding him when we disembarked.


00:35:44.024 --> 00:35:45.504
Yeah. I remember the photo.


00:35:46.626 --> 00:35:48.230
And the 60 Minutes interview.


00:35:49.462 --> 00:35:51.600
You were like Superwoman for a month.


00:35:51.997 --> 00:35:53.102
Yeah.


00:35:53.866 --> 00:35:56.403
Every time I tried to speak up, say,
"This is wrong,"


00:35:56.735 --> 00:35:58.714
military publicists kept saying,


00:35:59.070 --> 00:36:01.812
"Just go along with it.
Your country needs you.


00:36:01.873 --> 00:36:03.011
"You're an inspiration."


00:36:05.043 --> 00:36:06.817
How can you inspire people with lies?


00:36:09.246 --> 00:36:13.625
Honestly, I was relieved
when Claire Fallen exposed it all.


00:36:14.817 --> 00:36:18.060
I could never live up to
what they wanted from me.


00:36:18.754 --> 00:36:20.994
Wasn't even strong enough
to tell the truth.


00:36:22.457 --> 00:36:23.937
Yeah, well...


00:36:25.894 --> 00:36:27.999
At least you served in combat.


00:36:34.802 --> 00:36:38.214
I hope we don't find
anything crazy up there.


00:36:40.673 --> 00:36:41.981
Clear.


00:36:49.248 --> 00:36:50.318
No!


00:36:51.483 --> 00:36:54.225
- No.
- Colonel, we're trying to get...


00:36:55.753 --> 00:36:57.790
Come on, come on, come on. Let's go.


00:37:03.727 --> 00:37:05.331
Clear.


00:37:11.567 --> 00:37:13.046
Go!


00:37:13.836 --> 00:37:14.905
Go!


00:37:20.008 --> 00:37:21.180
Clear.


00:37:59.042 --> 00:38:01.113
- Let's go. Let's go! In.
- Come on! Let's go!


00:38:01.176 --> 00:38:02.416
Let's go! Let's go!


00:38:12.621 --> 00:38:14.600
Sam, grab those lights.


00:38:18.258 --> 00:38:19.465
Here.


00:38:29.735 --> 00:38:31.578
Colonel, what's going on?


00:38:32.370 --> 00:38:33.440
Quiet.


00:38:33.771 --> 00:38:36.115
What was in the vent?


00:38:41.144 --> 00:38:42.624
All right, come on.


00:39:10.837 --> 00:39:11.941
Kevin! Come on!


00:39:18.144 --> 00:39:19.247
Come on.


00:39:21.314 --> 00:39:22.690
This is it.


00:39:24.716 --> 00:39:25.956
That's the shot.


00:39:41.131 --> 00:39:42.609
Kevin!


00:39:45.834 --> 00:39:47.780
Kamecki!


00:40:05.217 --> 00:40:06.821
Shoot!


00:40:16.128 --> 00:40:17.663
Damn it.


00:40:21.565 --> 00:40:23.102
What the hell was that thing?


00:40:25.903 --> 00:40:27.439
The least of our problems.


00:40:33.476 --> 00:40:36.752
What did you mean earlier when
you said that thing about combat?


00:40:36.812 --> 00:40:38.690
I don't know what you're talking about.


00:40:38.948 --> 00:40:41.985
You said, "At least you served
in combat," like you hadn't.


00:40:42.784 --> 00:40:44.160
Is that what I said?


00:40:45.586 --> 00:40:47.566
Just because you accidentally
shot your foot doesn't...


00:40:47.621 --> 00:40:49.794
It wasn't an accident.


00:40:52.392 --> 00:40:54.373
I never even went to battle.


00:40:56.162 --> 00:40:58.335
I was so scared.


00:40:59.164 --> 00:41:03.442
I heard these voices saying,
"Don't do it. Don't do it."


00:41:05.571 --> 00:41:09.212
So I stepped off the carrier,
pointed the gun at my foot,


00:41:11.275 --> 00:41:15.780
and boom, back on the carrier,
back to safety.


00:41:17.181 --> 00:41:18.853
Nice work, huh?


00:41:19.883 --> 00:41:23.659
At least you set foot on the battlefield.
Some don't even make it that far.


00:41:24.654 --> 00:41:26.133
Did it ever hurt?


00:41:27.389 --> 00:41:28.459
Not there.


00:41:28.824 --> 00:41:30.860
- Attention!
- Yes, sir. Right away, sir.


00:41:34.028 --> 00:41:35.701
Shoes, drop everything.
You're coming with me.


00:41:35.763 --> 00:41:36.935
- Yes, Chief.
- Hannah?


00:41:36.998 --> 00:41:38.533
- Coming, Chief.
- No, you're not.


00:41:38.632 --> 00:41:40.704
You're staying up here in the hangar.


00:41:40.768 --> 00:41:42.974
- All due respect...
- I need a staff sergeant up top.


00:41:43.036 --> 00:41:45.346
Until I return, you're the ranking officer.


00:41:45.405 --> 00:41:46.974
Yes, Chief.


00:41:47.039 --> 00:41:49.350
Yes, sir. Affirmative.


00:41:49.642 --> 00:41:51.952
Back up through. Yes, sir.


00:41:52.011 --> 00:41:54.115
Yes, sir. Shoes, break the glass.


00:42:28.843 --> 00:42:30.186
Yes, sir.


00:42:52.196 --> 00:42:55.802
Looks like you're all about to jump six
levels of security clearance, Airmen.


00:42:56.099 --> 00:42:57.443
Stay sharp.


00:43:01.204 --> 00:43:06.278
If anything comes up here
that isn't human, kill it.


00:43:07.643 --> 00:43:08.781
Yes, Chief.


00:43:09.078 --> 00:43:12.149
Did he just say anything that comes up here
that isn't human?


00:43:12.414 --> 00:43:14.860
I knew it. I told you. I told you!


00:43:21.957 --> 00:43:24.698
All right, Airmen.
You've all been in combat, right?


00:43:24.758 --> 00:43:26.293
- Yes, Chief.
- Affirmative, Chief.


00:43:57.319 --> 00:43:58.856
What's this?


00:43:59.589 --> 00:44:01.465
Last resort.


00:44:17.037 --> 00:44:20.677
Damn it. Someone's calling the elevator
from down below.


00:44:20.740 --> 00:44:23.984
What do you mean down below?
You said there were only two levels.


00:44:53.069 --> 00:44:54.275
Oh, my God.


00:44:58.240 --> 00:44:59.775
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


00:45:02.310 --> 00:45:04.687
She's out. She's out.


00:45:06.514 --> 00:45:09.427
All right. Come on. Come on, buddy.
You're going to make it.


00:45:11.751 --> 00:45:17.861
Go on. Get out of here. Come on.
Come on. Come on. Come on.


00:45:41.144 --> 00:45:42.747
She's gone.


00:45:49.718 --> 00:45:51.288
No aliens in Area 51, Colonel?


00:45:53.754 --> 00:45:55.701
Yes, there are.


00:46:04.565 --> 00:46:06.100
J Rod.


00:46:10.636 --> 00:46:12.979
These must be our honored guests.


00:46:45.166 --> 00:46:46.770
What the hell could have done this?


00:46:49.137 --> 00:46:50.616
Nothing from this planet.


00:46:56.208 --> 00:46:57.745
Hold your fire.


00:47:27.068 --> 00:47:29.071
- We're clear.
- Clear.


00:47:35.343 --> 00:47:40.849
Blue dot, that's us.
Red dots, those are our targets.


00:47:41.815 --> 00:47:44.456
Targets? There's more than one?


00:47:46.452 --> 00:47:47.988
That way.


00:47:53.158 --> 00:47:54.637
Look alive.


00:47:55.294 --> 00:47:56.830
Listen up.


00:47:57.061 --> 00:48:00.975
We have to be prepared to send
another team down if they don't come back.


00:48:01.999 --> 00:48:06.038
And what? Just keep cranking up
the body count until no one's left?


00:48:06.938 --> 00:48:08.246
Is that your plan?


00:48:08.705 --> 00:48:10.946
If it is my plan,
you'll implement it without question.


00:48:11.007 --> 00:48:12.883
Is that a problem for you, Airman?


00:48:14.444 --> 00:48:15.479
No ma'am.


00:48:16.645 --> 00:48:18.784
- Here it comes.
- Here what comes? What is it?


00:48:18.848 --> 00:48:20.383
Hell if I know. Just shoot it!


00:48:33.460 --> 00:48:35.462
Did something just get on the elevator?


00:48:40.032 --> 00:48:42.103
Hannah, look alive.


00:48:42.168 --> 00:48:44.340
Something's coming up the elevator.


00:48:47.205 --> 00:48:51.050
Go! Go! In formation. Cover the elevator.
Go! Go! Go!


00:49:20.534 --> 00:49:22.069
Clear.


00:49:22.869 --> 00:49:25.441
- Why did it come up again?
- I don't know.


00:49:25.506 --> 00:49:27.041
- Are you sure it's clear?
- Yes.


00:49:27.107 --> 00:49:29.383
Well, why won't the door close?


00:49:29.775 --> 00:49:31.915
- James, that's enough.
- Something's wrong here, man.


00:49:32.012 --> 00:49:35.254
Elevators just don't come up.
I'm closing the door.


00:49:35.881 --> 00:49:37.587
James! Back in formation!


00:49:39.051 --> 00:49:40.325
Why isn't it working?


00:50:31.696 --> 00:50:33.699
Hannah, are you okay?


00:50:57.653 --> 00:50:59.427
You okay? Smith, are you okay?


00:51:00.688 --> 00:51:02.497
What's up?


00:51:04.726 --> 00:51:05.796
Baxter!


00:51:06.227 --> 00:51:08.433
I'm going to get that son of a bitch!


00:52:02.442 --> 00:52:04.080
We got it, guys!


00:52:04.244 --> 00:52:07.088
Yes! We got it! We got it!


00:52:09.148 --> 00:52:11.025
This is Staff Sergeant Hannah speaking.


00:52:11.083 --> 00:52:13.529
This is Colonel Ronald Martin.
I'm down on Level 3.


00:52:14.253 --> 00:52:16.254
I didn't know there was a Level 3.


00:52:16.654 --> 00:52:18.634
Sergeant Hannah, at the end of the day,


00:52:18.689 --> 00:52:21.329
you're gonna know a lot of things
that you didn't know before.


00:52:21.926 --> 00:52:24.565
Yes, sir. We killed that thing.


00:52:25.462 --> 00:52:28.067
We lost two men.
Another took friendly fire and I'm injured,


00:52:28.130 --> 00:52:29.542
so we're about half-strength.


00:52:29.599 --> 00:52:30.737
You're injured?


00:52:30.801 --> 00:52:33.838
Yeah. The thing took a little bite out
of me, but nothing serious.


00:52:33.903 --> 00:52:35.381
All right. Listen to me, Sergeant.


00:52:35.870 --> 00:52:37.873
You've been bitten by a Malaka Pod.


00:52:37.940 --> 00:52:41.113
The wound isn't fatal,
but Lady Death has also escaped.


00:52:41.176 --> 00:52:43.587
She's bigger, smarter and faster.


00:52:44.245 --> 00:52:47.054
If you encounter her, she's going to know
by the smell of your wound


00:52:47.114 --> 00:52:48.388
that you tangled with her baby.


00:52:48.782 --> 00:52:50.352
That thing was a baby?


00:52:50.417 --> 00:52:53.762
And we're trying to get back up top,
but we can't go the same way we came.


00:52:54.321 --> 00:52:56.163
The chief and his boys
are hunting for her down here,


00:52:56.222 --> 00:52:58.792
but if that all goes south,
you are the last line of defense.


00:52:59.057 --> 00:53:02.267
You cannot let her escape this base.
Is that clear?


00:53:03.462 --> 00:53:04.805
Yes, sir.


00:53:04.863 --> 00:53:06.364
All right. Good luck.


00:53:08.567 --> 00:53:11.172
We killed it. Yeah!


00:53:12.269 --> 00:53:14.578
- I can't believe it.
- Yeah, we did.


00:53:15.439 --> 00:53:16.747
On me.


00:53:22.077 --> 00:53:23.523
We need a plan.


00:53:26.648 --> 00:53:28.127
This is global.


00:53:33.454 --> 00:53:37.163
So, J Rod, tell us...
Tell us how you ended up here.


00:53:38.024 --> 00:53:41.972
My craft was accidentally struck
by a missile 60 years ago.


00:53:42.028 --> 00:53:45.736
My friends here at the base
are still trying to find me a way home.


00:53:45.798 --> 00:53:50.076
God, it's uncanny. He looks exactly
like those fake alien photos from the '50s.


00:53:50.169 --> 00:53:51.546
Those photos aren't fake.


00:53:52.304 --> 00:53:54.682
We haven't found out who leaked them yet.


00:53:55.541 --> 00:53:58.953
J Rod, have you seen
Patient Zero's vital screens?


00:53:59.978 --> 00:54:02.549
After waiting years for the right day
to escape,


00:54:02.614 --> 00:54:06.823
I find it unlikely that Patient Zero
would allow himself to be killed so easily.


00:54:07.117 --> 00:54:09.688
Well, if he is dead,
we'll need confirmation.


00:54:14.290 --> 00:54:15.291
How does this thing work?


00:54:15.358 --> 00:54:19.272
Patient Zero has a chip under
his skin to monitor vitals and location.


00:54:19.995 --> 00:54:22.407
All the alien life forms on
the premises are chipped.


00:54:22.464 --> 00:54:23.499
Except me.


00:54:24.966 --> 00:54:26.570
Yes, that's right.


00:54:27.068 --> 00:54:29.638
The moving red dot is Lady Death.


00:54:29.703 --> 00:54:32.205
One of the motionless red dots
is Little Devil.


00:54:32.740 --> 00:54:34.549
- The others...
- This is Colonel Martin.


00:54:35.441 --> 00:54:36.818
We have a new primary target.


00:54:36.876 --> 00:54:39.982
It looks like he's in the food
storage room, possibly terminated.


00:54:40.613 --> 00:54:42.058
Don't take any chances.


00:54:42.315 --> 00:54:43.384
Copy that, sir.


00:55:11.340 --> 00:55:13.616
It’s in here somewhere, Chief.


00:55:15.243 --> 00:55:16.779
Watch your asses.


00:55:18.212 --> 00:55:20.090
He's the most dangerous, isn't he?


00:55:21.015 --> 00:55:22.015
What?


00:55:22.282 --> 00:55:23.886
This Patient Zero.


00:55:25.185 --> 00:55:26.459
You're more worried about him


00:55:26.520 --> 00:55:30.433
than you are about the monster
that destroyed the elevator. Now, why?


00:55:30.590 --> 00:55:32.035
What can he do?


00:55:41.298 --> 00:55:43.438
J Rod, lock the door.


00:55:46.036 --> 00:55:49.813
In the interest of security, you will all
have to be tested before we move on.


00:55:49.873 --> 00:55:52.682
Lieutenant Kamecki, hand me your rifle.


00:55:54.277 --> 00:55:55.813
I'll cover you.


00:55:56.112 --> 00:55:58.820
What? Hang on. What's going on?


00:55:59.582 --> 00:56:02.858
Patient Zero can replicate other humanoids.


00:56:03.719 --> 00:56:05.699
There are ways of identifying him


00:56:05.754 --> 00:56:09.633
and since I don't want to have to cut
all of you to see if your blood is blue,


00:56:09.690 --> 00:56:12.933
I'll have Lieutenant Kamecki shine
alight in your eyes.


00:56:13.961 --> 00:56:17.100
If your pupils react, you are human.


00:56:18.498 --> 00:56:22.139
If not, I will blow you to hell.


00:56:36.147 --> 00:56:37.683
Chief?


00:56:45.188 --> 00:56:46.258
Clear.


00:57:11.611 --> 00:57:13.215
We're right on top of it.


00:57:20.319 --> 00:57:21.763
Clear.


00:57:29.726 --> 00:57:31.206
Wait a minute.


00:57:33.064 --> 00:57:35.873
This is ridiculous. I'm not an alien.


00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:38.536
You can't be serious.


00:57:38.902 --> 00:57:39.972
Deadly serious.


00:57:54.148 --> 00:57:55.218
Clear.


00:58:07.393 --> 00:58:08.929
What about you, Colonel?


00:58:10.796 --> 00:58:13.105
Shouldn't you and Lieutenant Kamecki
be tested?


00:58:16.735 --> 00:58:18.078
Yes. Of course.


00:58:20.971 --> 00:58:22.109
I don't shoot guns.


00:58:23.440 --> 00:58:24.976
I do.


00:58:49.964 --> 00:58:50.998
Clear.


00:59:43.377 --> 00:59:44.515
Why are you doing this?


00:59:46.712 --> 00:59:48.487
Why have you turned against our hosts?


00:59:51.484 --> 00:59:53.759
Have they not taken good care of you?


01:00:09.966 --> 01:00:11.036
He ditched the chip.


01:00:11.800 --> 01:00:13.280
Kamecki's dead.


01:00:13.470 --> 01:00:15.074
Yeah, I know.


01:00:26.314 --> 01:00:29.659
On me, men. Keep an eye on that thing.


01:00:29.951 --> 01:00:31.793
Let me know where the other one is.


01:00:31.852 --> 01:00:33.490
Chief, it's here.


01:00:34.554 --> 01:00:36.158
Chief, it's here.


01:00:37.691 --> 01:00:39.897
It’s on the ceiling! Fire!


01:00:57.541 --> 01:00:59.145
Oh, my God.


01:00:59.443 --> 01:01:00.888
I see it.


01:01:01.345 --> 01:01:03.415
Oh, my God! They're really here.


01:01:03.779 --> 01:01:05.690
What's here? Huh?


01:01:06.081 --> 01:01:07.652
What the hell was that thing...


01:01:23.531 --> 01:01:25.067
Travis!


01:01:27.567 --> 01:01:29.843
Travis! Travis!


01:01:38.443 --> 01:01:41.048
Chief! Chief, behind you!


01:02:19.545 --> 01:02:20.580
Yeah!


01:02:21.614 --> 01:02:24.220
All of the explosives.
If it goes boom, it goes in the Jeep.


01:02:24.283 --> 01:02:25.819
Aye, Sergeant.


01:02:25.885 --> 01:02:27.420
It’s okay, Smith. We got them.


01:02:28.820 --> 01:02:32.632
I swear we'll get you to a hospital
as soon as all this is over.


01:02:32.691 --> 01:02:35.364
Shouldn't we hold back a few grenades
in case it doesn't work?


01:02:35.793 --> 01:02:38.399
That little one almost took us apart.
This one's bigger.


01:02:38.729 --> 01:02:40.265
The way I see it, we got one shot.


01:02:40.331 --> 01:02:43.868
If this doesn't work, well, then
it doesn't matter what we do.


01:02:44.100 --> 01:02:45.636
Hang in there, Airman.


01:02:46.069 --> 01:02:47.707
Yes, ma'am.


01:02:48.738 --> 01:02:50.115
Chief, do you read me?


01:02:53.842 --> 01:02:56.550
Look, if we go up top,
we've got Lady Death on the loose.


01:02:56.645 --> 01:02:57.715
If we go down below...


01:02:57.779 --> 01:03:01.021
I do not understand why Patient Zero
infiltrated your group


01:03:01.082 --> 01:03:02.425
instead of leaving the base.


01:03:02.483 --> 01:03:05.362
Is there's something here
that he still wants?


01:03:07.120 --> 01:03:08.599
I don't know. I don't know.


01:03:08.855 --> 01:03:10.562
All I do know is that he's more powerful.


01:03:10.624 --> 01:03:12.331
I mean, how did he do that
with those boxes?


01:03:12.392 --> 01:03:15.531
If he has learned to simulate abilities
as well as appearance,


01:03:15.594 --> 01:03:17.835
he very well could have absorbed
this power from me.


01:03:17.896 --> 01:03:19.000
No way he can do that.


01:03:19.064 --> 01:03:20.805
We cannot be sure what he knows.


01:03:20.866 --> 01:03:24.176
He has had as much time to study us
as we have had to study him.


01:03:24.836 --> 01:03:27.942
We cannot let Patient Zero escape.


01:03:28.006 --> 01:03:30.349
But never mind him.
How are we going to escape?


01:03:30.741 --> 01:03:33.551
We have far more important things
to be concerned about right now.


01:03:33.610 --> 01:03:35.146
- If he escapes...
- Then what?


01:03:35.212 --> 01:03:37.953
If he gets out into the general population,
he disappears.


01:03:38.047 --> 01:03:41.028
Not long after that,
he'll have contacted his mother ship.


01:03:41.083 --> 01:03:43.120
- How do you know that?
- And then it'll only be a matter of time


01:03:43.185 --> 01:03:44.720
before there's a full-scale attack.


01:03:44.786 --> 01:03:46.288
How do you know that?


01:03:46.888 --> 01:03:50.893
Because we have had him for over 25 years.
I know every damn thing about it.


01:03:50.959 --> 01:03:52.733
Yeah, except for when he planned
to break out.


01:03:52.793 --> 01:03:55.797
- There is another issue to address, Colonel.
- What?


01:03:55.896 --> 01:03:58.843
The countdown self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.


01:03:58.899 --> 01:04:00.002
- What?
- What?


01:04:00.099 --> 01:04:02.010
Who would do that?


01:04:02.502 --> 01:04:04.448
Who would do that?


01:04:04.504 --> 01:04:06.006
It’s my superior, General Hammer.


01:04:06.072 --> 01:04:08.483
He's got the final word
on everything out here.


01:04:11.076 --> 01:04:13.488
Damn it! They're cutting us loose.


01:04:13.545 --> 01:04:14.615
Are you sure about this?


01:04:14.680 --> 01:04:17.626
I mean, why isn't the system
sending out evacuation alarms?


01:04:17.715 --> 01:04:19.752
Maybe your superior didn't want it to.


01:04:19.984 --> 01:04:22.658
We have just over 35 minutes
to escape detonation.


01:04:22.720 --> 01:04:25.393
- Thirty-five minutes?
- We've got to find Patient Zero first.


01:04:25.989 --> 01:04:28.299
Now, just let me think
and get out of my way.


01:04:49.710 --> 01:04:53.214
All right. The self-destruct sequence
was issued outside the base.


01:04:54.014 --> 01:04:55.549
That way I can't abort it.


01:04:56.348 --> 01:04:59.090
They'll have blocked all my access, but...


01:05:01.587 --> 01:05:05.227
Maybe... Maybe if you use my office
computer you could...


01:05:05.390 --> 01:05:08.098
You could circumvent the block
telekinetically.


01:05:08.226 --> 01:05:09.863
I believe that could work.


01:05:09.993 --> 01:05:11.370
Good!


01:05:12.096 --> 01:05:13.268
Good.


01:05:13.330 --> 01:05:15.867
Now, listen to me.
You try to access the system.


01:05:17.167 --> 01:05:21.138
Whether it works or not, you find
your way to the personnel elevator


01:05:21.204 --> 01:05:23.445
in 15 minutes and you join us, okay?


01:05:24.207 --> 01:05:26.083
- All right?
- I will, Colonel.


01:05:27.342 --> 01:05:30.619
- Let's go.
- Come on, people. This could work.


01:05:37.485 --> 01:05:38.862
Where are we going?


01:05:41.654 --> 01:05:43.133
Room 4118.


01:05:44.424 --> 01:05:45.960
Let's go.


01:05:48.560 --> 01:05:50.005
Keep it moving.


01:05:50.863 --> 01:05:52.342
What the hell are you doing up?


01:05:53.365 --> 01:05:56.470
The detonator's not remote. it's wired.


01:05:56.968 --> 01:05:58.504
So that means that somebody's
going to have to...


01:05:58.569 --> 01:06:00.515
- You can't.
- Yes, I can.


01:06:01.706 --> 01:06:04.151
And you and I both know
I'm not going to make it anyway.


01:06:04.808 --> 01:06:07.186
You were right, Claire.
We're all responsible for our own actions.


01:06:07.244 --> 01:06:09.690
Orders or not, it's up to me.


01:06:10.614 --> 01:06:15.119
Four decades of military service,
and if I've learned one thing,


01:06:15.518 --> 01:06:19.966
it's when all is said and done,
you're only accountable for one person.


01:06:21.523 --> 01:06:23.003
Yourself.


01:06:32.666 --> 01:06:34.872
They brought this from the armory.


01:06:35.401 --> 01:06:36.846
It’s called a popper.


01:06:38.204 --> 01:06:42.152
It fires a small explosive,
like a mini-crossbow bolt.


01:06:42.607 --> 01:06:45.850
You hit an arm or leg, you blow it off.


01:06:46.912 --> 01:06:49.620
It’s not big enough for the Jeep,
but it may come in handy.


01:06:49.815 --> 01:06:50.918
Thank you.


01:06:51.315 --> 01:06:52.794
You better get going.


01:06:56.053 --> 01:06:57.862
When did that elevator door close?


01:06:58.454 --> 01:07:02.266
Get to the Jeep. Go, everyone!
Now! On the Jeep!


01:07:02.425 --> 01:07:04.496
I've had enough of the secrets.


01:07:04.594 --> 01:07:07.039
Secrets that are killing my men
up there right now.


01:07:08.063 --> 01:07:10.407
It's time people knew the truth.
You up to it?


01:07:11.633 --> 01:07:15.637
Maybe not alone, but if we join forces
with Sam's level of influence...


01:07:15.903 --> 01:07:18.076
And Claire's reputation for integrity...


01:07:18.272 --> 01:07:20.752
Well, nobody would be able to cover
this story up.


01:07:23.176 --> 01:07:26.385
All right. You shoot everything.


01:07:33.586 --> 01:07:35.463
Hurry. She's in there all alone.


01:07:35.988 --> 01:07:37.159
Sixty seconds.


01:07:53.436 --> 01:07:54.540
Take this.


01:07:55.639 --> 01:07:57.208
I'm not going to be needing that.


01:09:07.968 --> 01:09:10.880
Yeah, that's right. I'm the one you want.


01:09:14.473 --> 01:09:15.679
Hurry!


01:09:16.208 --> 01:09:17.208
Hurry!


01:09:32.389 --> 01:09:34.299
Go! Take cover!


01:09:36.926 --> 01:09:40.100
Now! Now! Smith, now!


01:09:42.798 --> 01:09:46.302
Yeah! Come get me, you big ugly alien!


01:10:12.256 --> 01:10:13.564
Open fire!


01:11:30.091 --> 01:11:32.231
That's right. You better run!


01:11:34.429 --> 01:11:35.567
You okay?


01:11:38.365 --> 01:11:39.845
Yeah.


01:11:40.101 --> 01:11:41.909
You would figure they'd have some sort
of high-tech weapons


01:11:41.968 --> 01:11:44.107
that pop out of the ground
and take care of these damn things.


01:11:44.837 --> 01:11:46.339
They probably do.


01:11:46.405 --> 01:11:48.009
Then why aren't they using them?


01:11:48.407 --> 01:11:51.013
I guess someone values
these aliens' lives more than ours.


01:11:52.844 --> 01:11:54.380
We're going to have to do this ourselves.


01:12:27.541 --> 01:12:30.181
Got a back-up plan.
We have to time this thing out perfectly.


01:12:30.244 --> 01:12:31.620
What are you thinking?


01:12:31.845 --> 01:12:34.826
I don't know how long the signal's going
to last, so we better hurry.


01:12:36.616 --> 01:12:40.119
It’s me she wants.
So that's what we're going to give her.


01:13:57.586 --> 01:13:58.793
He's here.


01:14:00.589 --> 01:14:02.535
Come on. Let's go.


01:15:44.379 --> 01:15:46.757
Wait. Wait.


01:15:49.517 --> 01:15:50.518
Okay?


01:15:57.224 --> 01:15:58.601
It’s now or never.


01:15:58.659 --> 01:16:00.194
Go! Now!


01:16:23.780 --> 01:16:25.658
Now! Now!


01:16:41.496 --> 01:16:44.942
I don't want to hurt you.
There's been enough bloodshed already.


01:16:46.866 --> 01:16:47.867
Listen to me.


01:16:49.736 --> 01:16:53.979
If we stay, we all die. So please...


01:16:57.243 --> 01:16:59.779
You lied to me, Colonel.


01:17:01.180 --> 01:17:02.214
J Rod, please.


01:17:02.747 --> 01:17:06.092
You told me I was helping you
to understand your alien guests


01:17:06.150 --> 01:17:10.723
so you could send them all home.
Instead you made me a tool of your cruelty.


01:17:14.858 --> 01:17:16.269
We had to study your friend.


01:17:18.260 --> 01:17:21.070
So that we could better understand you.


01:17:21.464 --> 01:17:22.909
He died in the crash.


01:17:25.333 --> 01:17:27.006
Was the missile strike accidental?


01:17:27.737 --> 01:17:28.737
No.


01:17:39.146 --> 01:17:41.955
I'm sorry. it's over.


01:17:43.717 --> 01:17:45.855
Look, whatever happened, I'm sorry.


01:17:47.953 --> 01:17:48.954
No.


01:17:49.054 --> 01:17:52.831
We're going to expose the truth
about this whole place.


01:17:52.891 --> 01:17:53.892
I do not believe you.


01:18:00.364 --> 01:18:02.037
It’s true! it's true!


01:18:02.099 --> 01:18:04.442
He told us. He wants to show
the world what's happening here.


01:18:04.501 --> 01:18:06.175
He's going to help us expose this place.


01:18:06.737 --> 01:18:09.046
This man is not to be trusted.


01:18:09.406 --> 01:18:11.885
My camera is destroyed.
We need the Colonel.


01:18:13.075 --> 01:18:16.113
Without his protection,
you will be captured and silenced.


01:18:16.178 --> 01:18:18.658
Don't you see? You have to trust us.


01:18:19.414 --> 01:18:21.554
We have to tell them what's happening here!


01:18:24.485 --> 01:18:26.396
Please! Please!


01:18:36.162 --> 01:18:37.198
No!


01:18:53.577 --> 01:18:54.783
Are you okay?


01:18:56.113 --> 01:18:57.591
Sam?


01:18:58.781 --> 01:19:00.056
Sam, you okay?


01:19:00.117 --> 01:19:02.824
Yeah. I think so.


01:19:24.637 --> 01:19:25.877
Something's wrong.


01:19:26.706 --> 01:19:27.912
Cover me.


01:19:28.941 --> 01:19:29.976
Ready?


01:19:48.358 --> 01:19:49.428
Damn it.


01:19:53.229 --> 01:19:54.334
He got away.


01:19:57.733 --> 01:19:59.110
Oh, God, Sam.


01:20:00.535 --> 01:20:02.140
Can you walk?


01:20:03.137 --> 01:20:04.172
Yeah.


01:20:05.607 --> 01:20:07.142
Hannah! Hannah!


01:20:09.376 --> 01:20:10.378
Hannah.


01:20:11.512 --> 01:20:12.718
Hey.


01:20:13.580 --> 01:20:15.320
- Did you get it?
- Yeah.


01:20:17.083 --> 01:20:18.119
Come on.


01:20:21.621 --> 01:20:23.099
Are you okay?


01:20:23.154 --> 01:20:25.157
Can you walk? Come on.


01:20:26.625 --> 01:20:28.866
I think I broke my arm for real this time.


01:20:30.694 --> 01:20:32.173
Airmen don't cry.


01:20:32.898 --> 01:20:34.501
They bleed tears.


01:20:42.238 --> 01:20:44.775
Patient Zero's still somewhere
in the compound.


01:20:44.841 --> 01:20:47.286
I failed to abort the
self-destruct sequence.


01:20:47.342 --> 01:20:49.186
- We are still in danger.
- Oh, my God.


01:20:49.778 --> 01:20:52.987
All right.
Personnel elevator should still work.


01:20:53.215 --> 01:20:56.355
Let's just hope he doesn't know about it yet.
Come on, follow me.


01:20:56.485 --> 01:20:57.895
Come on, Sam.


01:20:57.985 --> 01:21:00.431
Hang in there.
We're going to get you out of here.


01:21:11.631 --> 01:21:13.166
Can we make it in time, Colonel?


01:21:15.100 --> 01:21:19.014
If absolutely nothing else
goes wrong, maybe.


01:21:19.872 --> 01:21:21.077
Nothing else...


01:21:21.539 --> 01:21:24.712
Lady Death could be up there,
the vehicles could be destroyed,


01:21:24.808 --> 01:21:26.880
Patient Zero could be waiting to ambush us.


01:21:28.979 --> 01:21:30.583
Yeah.


01:21:47.695 --> 01:21:48.765
Did you kill her?


01:21:48.862 --> 01:21:50.467
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.


01:21:51.333 --> 01:21:52.868
Good work.


01:21:53.067 --> 01:21:57.014
Come on. We've got less than 10 minutes
before this whole place goes up.


01:21:57.103 --> 01:21:59.481
Our most dangerous resident
is still at large.


01:22:00.106 --> 01:22:01.551
If he gets off the grounds,


01:22:01.608 --> 01:22:04.486
we'll have to set up check points,
road blocks.


01:22:05.043 --> 01:22:07.114
We cannot let him escape, people!


01:22:11.582 --> 01:22:13.187
Colonel, who are you calling?


01:22:14.919 --> 01:22:16.398
General Hammer.


01:22:19.990 --> 01:22:21.402
She'll know what to do.


01:22:36.405 --> 01:22:39.044
Sam, what did you do?


01:22:42.509 --> 01:22:43.852
He's an alien! Shoot him!


01:22:44.612 --> 01:22:45.612
I'm out!


01:23:02.994 --> 01:23:04.667
It ends here, Patient Zero.


01:23:25.580 --> 01:23:26.581
Thank you.


01:23:31.720 --> 01:23:33.995
You okay? You okay?


01:23:38.159 --> 01:23:39.831
We now have seven minutes.


01:23:41.061 --> 01:23:43.836
Come on! Everybody in. Let's go! Come on!


01:24:16.491 --> 01:24:18.267
Go, go, go! Just go!


01:24:19.461 --> 01:24:20.872
I'm driving as fast as I can.


01:24:20.929 --> 01:24:24.307
I recommend a higher rate of speed
to avoid the fallout.


01:24:24.365 --> 01:24:26.742
- Never mind.
- Just go! Get out of here. Go!


01:24:47.218 --> 01:24:51.189
The Air Force and the Pentagon would not
comment on the footage that you just saw.


01:24:51.589 --> 01:24:54.660
Nor will they comment on the whereabouts
or even confirm


01:24:54.724 --> 01:24:57.796
that Miss Fallen and Mr. Whitaker
and their crews were there.


01:24:58.294 --> 01:25:01.536
I was there, though.
And I witnessed the most incredible


01:25:01.630 --> 01:25:04.805
and unbelievable explosion
that I've ever seen.


01:25:04.900 --> 01:25:08.541
Not to mention covering the biggest story
I've ever covered.


01:25:08.670 --> 01:25:12.243
Actually, you're about to top it.


01:25:13.040 --> 01:25:15.077
Claire Fallen, you made it out!


01:25:15.143 --> 01:25:17.850
Yeah, and I brought some friends with me.


01:25:21.548 --> 01:25:24.154
I imagine you have questions for me.


01:25:26.386 --> 01:25:28.524
People need to know the truth.


01:25:36.227 --> 01:25:37.604
Don't go away.


01:25:37.695 --> 01:25:40.641
We'll be right back with
this exclusive interview.

